{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 133, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the 0->3 identity shortcut where none exists restores the residual path and gives much larger gains than replacing an existing conv or pool there."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-to-output skip removes the cell's residual connection, which hurts far more than deleting a conv on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1->3 already absent, removing edge 0->3 leaves very few paths into the output node, which badly degrades trainability."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 is disconnected from the input, edge 0->3 is one of the only remaining routes to the output, so removing it is especially damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When there is no 0->3 shortcut, a skip on 2->3 supplies an alternative short gradient path, so the edit helps more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the first edge with a 3x3 conv adds useful capacity, a larger gain than swapping out skip, 1x1 conv, or none."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a harmful avg_pool on edge 0 costs little or helps, whereas removing a conv or skip there loses useful signal."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a pooling op on edge 1->3 for a 3x3 conv converts a weak edge into a strong one, giving larger gains than replacing none, skip, or 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing avg_pool on edge 0->2 with a 3x3 conv adds learnable features where pooling contributed little, so it beats replacing skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a skip on the final edge into pooling costs little, while turning a conv into pooling removes important capacity right before the output."}], "tok": 17776, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [[